ore ways to earn are listed on the page: refer a friend with your link (you both get points at their first rental), follow us, review your rental on carmacars.ca, review us on Google (press <b class="gd-ui">I posted my review</b> and give the name on it), a damage-free rental, your birthday and your first rental.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Get my code</b> turns points into a code of your own, from 500 points. Type it in the promo code box of your request. An unused code can be given back for the points.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Your tier comes from the points you earned in the last 12 months (using points never lowers it): <b class="gd-ui">Gold</b> from 1,000 points gives Instant Book (your request is booked at once), <b class="gd-ui">Platinum</b> from 15,000 gives <b class="gd-ui">Any car, any time</b> (request a car even on dates it shows as taken; we answer within 4 hours), <b class="gd-ui">Black</b> from 60,000 gives one free rental day a year as a code. Each tier keeps the perks below it. The bar shows how many points to the next tier.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Your discounts</b> lists every code you hold (from points, your tier, referrals, our team, the free day): what it gives, when it ends, and whether it is unused, on a request or used, with <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b>. When you send a request, tap the code under <b class="gd-ui">Use a saved discount</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Points end 12 months after your last rental or redemption. We email you a month before.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-your-trip-in-your-calendar-or-wallet" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your trip in your calendar or wallet</h2><p class="gd-p">On a confirmed booking, <b class="gd-ui">Add to calendar</b> adds the pickup and the return. The confirmation email has the same link. <b class="gd-ui">Add to Apple Wallet</b> shows when it is available.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-phone-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Get an alert on your phone or computer when your offer is ready, before pickup and return, for payments and when we message you, even with CarmaCars closed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>. Under <b class="gd-ui">Phone alerts</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Turn on alerts</b> and allow notifications when your browser asks.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">What to alert me about</b>, untick anything you do not want. Your choice applies to all your devices.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send a test alert</b> to see one. <b class="gd-ui">Turn off on this device</b> stops them there; <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes another device off.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">On iPhone and iPad, add CarmaCars to your Home Screen first: in Safari tap <b class="gd-ui">Share</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Add to Home Screen</b>. Open CarmaCars from your Home Screen, sign in and turn alerts on in Profile (iOS 16.4 or later).</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Alerts come as well as your emails and texts, never instead of them. Alerts that are not urgent wait until 8 am. Sign-in links and codes never come as alerts.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-delete-my-account" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Delete my account</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b> and scroll to <b class="gd-ui">Delete my account</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Delete my account</b>, add a reason if you like, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, delete my account</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">We settle anything still open (a rental, a deposit), delete your account and email you within 30 days. Changed your mind before then? Press <b class="gd-ui">Keep my account</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>We keep rental agreements, receipts and tax records as the law requires. Everything else, including your licence and selfie photos, is deleted.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-odometer-and-fuel-at-pickup-and-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Odometer and fuel at pickup and return</h2><p class="gd-p">When you check the car in or out yourself:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Add a photo of the dashboard (the odometer and the fuel gauge). It can come from your camera roll. We read it and ask, for example, &quot;Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Yes, correct</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">No, I will type it</b> and type the odometer and pick the fuel level.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Take a selfie in front of the car with your camera.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">After the return, <b class="gd-ui">Your return: km and fuel</b> on your booking shows the km driven, the km included and any km over, the fuel compared with pickup, and the charge for each. The photo report shows both dashboard photos.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-earn-reward-points" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Earn reward points</h2><p class="gd-p">Review your rental (add a photo for extra points), review us on Google, follow us from your Rewards page, refer a friend, and every rental after your first earns points too. See them all on <b class="gd-ui">Rewards</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-rewards-and-fuel-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rewards and fuel (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Earn points for a photo with your review and for every rental after your first; every way to earn is on your Rewards page.</li><li>A fuel shortfall at the return is priced from the car&#39;s tank and the local pump price, plus a refuelling fee, and checked by our team before any charge.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-thank-the-team" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Thank the team</h2><p class="gd-p">Happy with the service? On your booking after the return, or from the link in the &quot;Returned&quot; email, press <b class="gd-ui">Add a tip for the team</b>: 10, 15 or 20% or any amount, by card. It goes to the people who looked after your rental.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="after-your-trip-choose-your-notifications-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Choose your notifications (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b> lists each kind of notification we send you, with a switch for <b class="gd-ui">Push</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Email</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>. A switch is saved the moment you move it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">How often</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Instant</b> sends each one as it happens. <b class="gd-ui">Daily summary</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Weekly summary</b> holds the optional emails and sends them as one email in the morning.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Quiet hours</b>: turn them on and set the times. Optional phone alerts and texts wait until the quiet hours end.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Turn every optional notification off</b> stops them all at once. You still see every message in your portal.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The kinds under <b class="gd-ui">Always on</b> cannot be switched off: security and sign-in codes, legal and agreement notices, charges and fees, receipts, booking confirmations and changes, pickup and return reminders, and safety messages.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">If a text cannot be sent, the same message comes by email instead, so nothing is lost.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('owner', 'bookings-and-your-own-use', 'chapter', 'home-and-your-vehicles', 'See every booking in your cars on a calendar, and book a car for yourself when it is free.

## See your bookings

1. Cars > Bookings shows two months of your cars on a calendar. Each block is a booking number.
2. All bookings lists every trip with its car, dates, amount and status.

![](/guides/img/owner-04-calendar-desktop-be31cbae.jpg "desktop; size: 980 1092; address: carmacars.ca/owner/bookings; pins: 1 53.1 15.8, 2 12.2 94.5")

> Good to know: A booking can show as Booked, with its dates and no amount: its amounts show once we approve the statement that covers it, and your statement carries every booking you can see, and every booking paid by the renter. The only bookings left out are an insurance replacement we hide from you and an insurer-billed rental that does not block your car''s calendar: they are not part of your revenue, so they stay off your statements and payouts, and you see only that the car is unavailable for those dates. If one of them later starts counting, you get the new booking email then. Unavailable is time your car is in use by us with no revenue for you (for example an insurance hold). A booking expense or a Revenue Share set for one booking is listed on that booking with the reason, and on your statement.

## Rental history

Cars > Bookings also has the **Rental history**: every rental on your cars.

1. Each line: the booking number, the car and its plate, the pickup and the return, the days, the status and your earnings from your approved statements. Not on an approved statement yet: it says so.
2. Choose one car or all, and oldest or newest first. The totals at the top count every rental in the list.
3. Renter details, payments and deposits are never shown, and a cancelled booking is listed only when a charge was kept.

## Book your own car

You pay no rental charge, fee or deposit. A renter''s confirmed booking comes first.

1. Open Cars > Bookings and use **Book my own car** on the right (or **Book it for myself** on the car''s page).
2. Choose the Vehicle, then the Pickup and Return date and time.
3. Add a Note (optional) for our team.
4. Press **Book my car**. You sign the same agreement a renter signs.

![](/guides/img/owner-04-calendar-desktop-a4500851.jpg "desktop; size: 450 570; address: carmacars.ca/owner/bookings; pins: 2 92.2 14.6, 3 92.2 64.9, 4 42.2 89.6")

> Good to know: No price and no deposit apply to you. One booking can be 30 days at most, and you sign the rental agreement before pickup.

## Rideshare and repeat renters (release 35)

Renters may drive for rideshare and delivery platforms with the documents we issue. Verified repeat renters can book your car instantly when it is free, within your price limits.', 'Bookings and your own use', 'The bookings calendar and booking your own car.',
  'See every booking in your cars on a calendar, and book a car for yourself when it is free.

## See your bookings

1. Cars > Bookings shows two months of your cars on a calendar. Each block is a booking number.
2. All bookings lists every trip with its car, dates, amount and status.

![](/guides/img/owner-04-calendar-desktop-be31cbae.jpg "desktop; size: 980 1092; address: carmacars.ca/owner/bookings; pins: 1 53.1 15.8, 2 12.2 94.5")

> Good to know: A booking can show as Booked, with its dates and no amount: its amounts show once we approve the statement that covers it, and your statement carries every booking you can see, and every booking paid by the renter. The only bookings left out are an insurance replacement we hide from you and an insurer-billed rental that does not block your car''s calendar: they are not part of your revenue, so they stay off your statements and payouts, and you see only that the car is unavailable for those dates. If one of them later starts counting, you get the new booking email then. Unavailable is time your car is in use by us with no revenue for you (for example an insurance hold). A booking expense or a Revenue Share set for one booking is listed on that booking with the reason, and on your statement.

## Rental history

Cars > Bookings also has the **Rental history**: every rental on your cars.

1. Each line: the booking number, the car and its plate, the pickup and the return, the days, the status and your earnings from your approved statements. Not on an approved statement yet: it says so.
2. Choose one car or all, and oldest or newest first. The totals at the top count every rental in the list.
3. Renter details, payments and deposits are never shown, and a cancelled booking is listed only when a charge was kept.

## Book your own car

You pay no rental charge, fee or deposit. A renter''s confirmed booking comes first. Any car still in the program can be booked, a car still onboarding too; if one cannot be booked on your dates (out of service, or a renter has it), the form says why.

1. Open Cars > Bookings and use **Book my own car** on the right (or **Book it for myself** on the car''s page).
2. Choose the Vehicle, then the Pickup and Return date and time.
3. Who''s driving? Choose Me, or Someone else for a family member or friend: add their full name, email, phone and date of birth. They are the main driver: they get their own link to add their licence and a selfie and to sign the rental agreement (the main driver needs an Ontario licence). You sign too.
4. Add a Note (optional) for our team.
5. Tick that you are responsible for the booking: the deductible ($2,500) and any damage, tickets, tolls and fees during it are billed to you, whoever drives, each with its evidence.
6. Press **Book my car**.

![](/guides/img/owner-04-calendar-desktop-a4500851.jpg "desktop; size: 450 570; address: carmacars.ca/owner/bookings; pins: 2 92.2 14.6, 3 92.2 64.9, 4 42.2 89.6")

> Good to know: An owner booking earns no revenue and is not on your statement. No price and no deposit apply to you. One booking can be 30 days at most, and you sign the rental agreement before pickup.

## Rideshare and repeat renters (release 35)

Renters may drive for rideshare and delivery platforms with the documents we issue. Verified repeat renters can book your car instantly when it is free, within your price limits.',
