 it? The invoice shows Partly paid and only the rest is debited.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-tell-us-where-to-pay-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tell us where to pay you</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Account</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Banking</b>. Under Where we pay you, choose Bank transfer or e-Transfer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Fill in Account holder, Institution number, Transit number and Account number (or your e-Transfer email).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Submit payout details</b>. For your security we confirm new details by phone before we use them.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/banking</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:990/642"><img src="/guides/img/owner-07-banking-desktop-87b2ffe3.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="990" height="642"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50.5%;top:25.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:90.9%;top:45.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:30.3%;top:89.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-statements-and-payouts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Statements and payouts</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">This month so far, at the top of Statements: the rentals finished this month, your Owner Revenue, the Revenue Share, fees and deductions and the expected payout, worked out live and marked Provisional. Rentals still under way are listed below it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Statements: one a month, once approved by CarmaCars; the approved statement is the final one. Open one to see each booking that counts toward your revenue (a booking paid by the renter always does; an insurance replacement we hide from you and an insurer-billed rental that does not block your calendar are left out), the revenue share, deductions and the payout.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Download PDF</b> to keep a copy. We also email it to you with the PDF attached.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Payouts shows what was paid to you and when. Payouts are made on the 10th for the month before.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/statements/380cc1bb-bfd5-4e55-8022-93a3b998ca74</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/792"><img src="/guides/img/owner-09-statement-desktop-fc5f9ea5.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="792"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:16%;top:30.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:66%;top:40.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Paid a flat monthly payment for a car? Its statement shows a Flat monthly payment line for the month (a part month by the day) instead of the Revenue Share. The car&#39;s rentals are listed without amounts paid to you, as CarmaCars keeps them, and there is no insurance or tracker fee for it. A booking expense is taken off only when we charge it to you; it then shows as an owner cost with its reason. Vehicles shows the amount and since when.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Fees taken from your statement</h3><p class="gd-p">If you agreed with CarmaCars to have your fees taken from your revenue statement, your invoices are not debited from your bank account. Each invoice is paid from your next owner statement (the line &quot;Invoice INV-..., paid from statement&quot;) and reads <b class="gd-ui">Paid from statement</b>. If a statement does not cover it, the rest is taken from the next one; an invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date is debited from your bank account after the usual notice.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">A flat monthly payment and your agreement</h3><p class="gd-p">If your cars are paid a flat monthly amount, your Enrollment Agreement is the <b class="gd-ui">Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement</b>: a fixed Monthly Amount per car on the payout date, part months by the day, no revenue share and no insurance or tracker fee. When your pay changes from one way to the other, Home shows <b class="gd-ui">Check and sign</b> for the new agreement.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-repairs-and-partner-credits" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Repairs and partner credits</h2><p class="gd-p">If CarmaCars turns it on for you, <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Statements</b> also shows the repair costs and partner credits on your own cars this year, with who paid each repair. It is not part of your statements or payouts.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-statement-periods-and-price-limits-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Statement periods and price limits (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Each statement covers the 8th of one month to the 7th of the next, and the payout on the 10th pays it. A rental across the cutoff is paid for the days in each period, never twice.</li><li>Amounts a renter still owes are listed apart on your statement and paid on the statement after we collect them.</li><li>Set the lowest and highest daily rate for every car or one car: short-notice pricing, promo codes, discounts and our offers stay between them.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-your-forecast-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your forecast (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Home</b> has a <b class="gd-ui">Forecast</b> section: the next 12 months of each of your cars, with its projected occupancy and projected owner revenue (before fees). Open a car to see its months; with several cars, the line on top adds them up.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Every car starts from the GTA&#39;s rental season: January and February are quiet, March Break and the long weekends pick up, July and August are the busiest, and December brings holiday travel.</li><li>Once a car has 3 full months on the program, its own occupancy is blended in, and it counts for more each month: half after 3 months, two thirds after 6, four fifths after 12. Under each car you see how its forecast is made.</li><li>Projected owner revenue uses your car&#39;s own statements of the last 12 months, per day booked; a newer car uses its daily rate less the Revenue Share.</li><li>Bookings hidden from you are never counted.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Each statement also has a <b class="gd-ui">Forecast</b> line: whether next month is projected higher or lower than the statement&#39;s month, by how many points of occupancy and about how much owner revenue, and why (the season).</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Note</span><div>A forecast is an estimate, not a promise. Your statements and payouts are always what your car actually earned.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-charges-on-your-own-bookings-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Charges on your own bookings (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">When you book your own car, for yourself or for someone else, you are responsible for what happens during it: damage up to the deductible, tickets, tolls, fuel, kilometres, cleaning, smoking, a late return and any other fee.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each charge is added only with its evidence (photos, readings, the notice or the receipt). You get an email that lists each charge and the evidence it rests on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">It is due at once. We charge the card you have on file. If you have no card on file, we start a pre-authorized debit from your bank account the same day.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">If there is no payment method on file, or the charge fails, you get an invoice with a <b class="gd-ui">pay</b> link, and reminders.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">An invoice still unpaid after 7 days, or at the next statement cut-off (the 7th) if that comes first, is deducted from your next statement as its own line.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fees-payments-and-payouts-late-fee-on-unpaid-insurance-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Late Fee on unpaid insurance (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">If your insurance is not paid on time (the debit on the 15th fails, or the invoice is unpaid after its due date), a Late Fee of 5% of the unpaid insurance is added to that invoice once, plus HST on the fee. Insurance itself has no HST.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">You get a reminder 3 days before the due date while the invoice is unpaid, and an email when the fee is added.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The unpaid insurance and the Late Fee are deducted from your next statement by themselves, as two separate lines. You can pay the invoice from its page before that.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">This replaces the $50 Late Fee for insurance. It is in section 4.4 and Schedule B of your agreement; you accept the update in the box that opens, without signing again.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('owner', 'rewards', 'chapter', 'fees-payments-and-payouts', null, 'Rewards', 'Your discounts, your friends and family code, credits and merch kits.',
  '**Rewards** in the menu shows everything you get as an owner, with your codes, your progress and your history.

## While your car is out

1. On dates your own car is on rent, in service or in a claim, your code gives you 20% off another CarmaCars car. Press **Copy the code**, then **Find a car**, and type the code in the promo code box of your request.
2. You are the driver. The licence check, the rental agreement and the deposit are the same as for any renter. The code does not work on exotic cars, partner cars or your own car.
3. If your car is being repaired for something CarmaCars caused, press **Ask for a free upgrade**, choose the car and say what happened. An Admin answers on this page and by email. When it is approved you get a one-time code.

## Friends and family

1. Share your **code**, your **link** or your **QR code**. A friend gets 10% off their first rental.
2. You earn 20% of the rental charge on that first rental. It shows on your statement once the trip is complete.
3. The page counts the friends who rented and what you earned.

## Refer an owner

Share the link under **Refer an owner**. When the owner you referred has had a car live for 30 days, a $100 credit goes on your next statement as its own line.

## Merch kits

1. At 6 months with CarmaCars the **CarmaCars merch kit** is ready, and at 12 months the **Premium merch kit**. The bar shows how far you are.
2. Nothing is sent by itself. Press **Redeem my merch kit**, check the address, choose a shirt size and press **Confirm and redeem**.
3. The kit then shows **Getting ready**, and **Shipped** with the tracking number once it is on its way. We email you at each step.

## Birthday credit and perks

1. On your birthday you get a $25 rental credit as a code, good for 60 days. Add your birthday under Account if we do not have it.
2. You have priority support: your calls, texts and messages are answered first. You also hear about new programs before anyone else.

**Your rewards so far** lists every credit, kit and code. Credits are a line on your statement. Your Revenue Share and fees do not change.',
