3. **The bar for Sales**: a Sales applicant passes the AI interview at or over the bar (Interview settings, 80 by default) with no knock-out answer, English not basic and no answer under 4 out of 10; the AI''s recommendation no longer declines a Sales applicant over the bar. Sales applicants declined that way in the last 30 days were decided again. Auto-hire still needs a passed AI interview.
4. A red box says when a WhatsApp group link is empty: nobody can join until you set it in **Settings** > **Program**.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Candidates apply on carmacars.ca/careers. Every application is scored on the server against the role&#39;s rubric: a candidate who passes gets a link to book a 15-minute call, one who does not qualify for Field staff is offered Sales instead, and the rest wait for you. During each call you fill in a rubric; the final score ranks everyone in the role.</p><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-open-a-role-and-send-the-apply-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Open a role and send the apply link</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Roles and links.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Open the role</b> to put it on carmacars.ca/careers (and in the sitemap and the footer); <b class="gd-ui">Close the role</b> takes it off. Field staff, Sales in person and Remote sales start open; the three remote assistant roles start closed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Copy the apply link: it ends with ?src=indeed (or ?src=onlinejobs for the remote roles), so each application records where it came from.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Copy the message under it and paste it into Indeed (or OnlineJobs.ph) messages to each applicant. It asks them to answer the role&#39;s questions, about five minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Pass mark and pay</b> changes the pass mark (60 of 100 unless you change it) and the pay shown on the page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-what-happens-to-each-application" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What happens to each application</h2><p class="gd-p">The database scores the answers the moment they arrive. The candidate never sees the points.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Score at or above the pass mark, no knock-out: an email with a personal link to book a call (Invited). A remote assistant (customer service, fleet, finance, remote sales) gets a link to a recorded AI interview instead, while AI interviews are on (see below).</li><li>Field staff who do not qualify (no full G licence, under three years of driving, or a low score) are not declined: they get a friendly email offering Sales in person, with a one-click link that fills in their details, and Remote sales named as the other choice (Referred). If they already applied for Sales, nothing is sent and a note says so. The email&#39;s button is <b class="gd-ui">Yes, put me in Sales</b>: one press makes their Sales application from the one they sent (no new form) and sends the AI interview link at once.</li><li>Sales in person below the pass mark, or remote only, is offered Remote sales. A remote assistant role below the pass mark is offered the closest other open role.</li><li>A knock-out with no other role to offer (for example the finance code word missing) gets a polite decline.</li><li>Anyone else waits for you as Below the bar, with only a confirmation email.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-review-the-applications" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review the applications</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Applications.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by role, status, source (Indeed, OnlineJobs.ph, website, referral) or score. Open a candidate for every answer with the points it earned and any knock-out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Invite anyway</b> sends the booking link to a candidate below the bar, declined or referred. <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> sends the polite decline email (untick it to decline without an email).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A candidate referred to another role shows the link both ways under Linked applications.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-days" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview days</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Interview days.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add an interview day</b>: the day, from and to (Toronto time), the call length (15 minutes) and the break between calls (5 minutes), phone or video, and the roles it is for (empty: every role).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Phone: you call the candidate on the number they gave. Video: every booking gets its own Jitsi Meet link, in the candidate&#39;s email and on their page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Candidates book, move or cancel from their link. They get a confirmation, a reminder the evening before and one an hour before (and a text, when phone and texts are on). Remote roles show Manila time too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> stops new bookings on a day; a day with bookings cannot be deleted.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-run-the-calls-with-the-rubric" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Run the calls with the rubric</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Calls.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Pick the day. Each call shows the time, the candidate, Call (or the video link). Press <b class="gd-ui">Start</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The rubric sits beside the call guide (what to ask each minute, and what a good answer sounds like). Score each line 1 to 5: Communication, Reliability and availability, Role skills, Customer or sales instinct, Judgement on the scenarios, Attitude.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the decision (Hire, Maybe, No, No show), add notes and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rubric</b>. The interview score (of 100) and the final score (40% screening, 60% interview) fill in, with the rank in the role.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-shortlist-and-hire" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Shortlist and Hire</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Shortlist.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each role lists its interviewed candidates by final score, rank 1 first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open the candidate and press <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b>. A short form opens: the <b class="gd-ui">Role</b> (customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person, Sales remote or field work), the <b class="gd-ui">Start date</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Pay</b>, filled in with the role&#39;s standard (a month in US dollars for an assistant, an hour in Canadian dollars for field work, commission only for Sales with its tiers). Change the pay if you agreed another.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm: hire and start onboarding</b>. One confirm does it all: the staff sign-in and its invitation email, the staff agreement sent to sign in their portal, the request for their pay details, the academy path of their role with the gate on, their first-day To do&#39;s on the start date (and one for you), and the candidate marked hired with the welcome email (release 44: no start date in it; training and claiming shifts only, then a hello in the team chat and the member tag &quot;Name - Position&quot; in each WhatsApp group, also a first-day To do); their call slot and AI interview link close.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding</b> card on the candidate shows each step: Done, Waiting or To do. A field hire&#39;s agreement waits for their home address and licence number: once they are in their profile, press <b class="gd-ui">Send the agreement</b>. When they enter their pay details, you get a To do: check them with the hire (a call or a message they started), write how, and press <b class="gd-ui">Verify</b>. Only the last 4 digits of an account number are ever shown.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Not hired</b> closes a candidate after the call without an email; <b class="gd-ui">Withdrawn</b> is for one who no longer wants the role.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Applications are for Admins only. The name, contact details and answers of a candidate who is not hired are deleted 12 months after the decision, as the privacy policy says.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A candidate who passes while no interview day is open for their role is invited but waits: the invitation email goes when you add (or open) a day for that role. The Hiring page shows &quot;N applicants invited but no interview day is open for&quot; the role, with <b class="gd-ui">Add an interview day</b>. Candidates who already had the email, or opened their link and found no time (&quot;No call times are open right now&quot;), get &quot;New times are open&quot; when the day is added.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-decisions-and-the-emails-they-send" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Decisions and the emails they send</h2><p class="gd-p">The rubric&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Decision</b> is Hire, Maybe, No, <b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b> or No show. Recording one sends nothing.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b> refers the candidate to Sales: Sales in person for Field staff and Sales in person, Remote Sales for the remote roles. If they already applied for that Sales role, their Sales application gets a note for the shortlist and no email goes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Emails to send</b>: every decided candidate with the email that will go (Hire: the next steps; Sales: the offer with the one-click apply link; No: the polite decline; No show: the polite no-show email). Maybe sends nothing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Change</b> a row (the decision, the email on or off, a personal line for the hire and no-show emails) or <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> it (the rubric goes back to Maybe).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send all decision emails</b>. Choose <b class="gd-ui">Now</b>, next Monday at 9:00 am Toronto, tomorrow at 9:00 am, or another time. Each candidate gets one email, never twice; the statuses follow (referred, Not hired, No show). To hire, press <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> on the candidate: it sends the welcome email itself, with the next steps.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-ai-interviews-for-the-remote-roles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">AI interviews for the remote roles</h2><p class="gd-p">Remote assistants who pass screening take a short interview on video on their own, from their phone or computer, instead of a live call. In-person roles keep their phone calls. <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Roles and links, card AI interviews for the remote roles: <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> sends the remote roles the booking link again. <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b>: Answer time (1 to 3 minutes, 2 by default), Retakes allowed (none by default) and Keep interview videos (90 days by default, then deleted).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The candidate gets one email, <b class="gd-ui">Start my interview</b>. The link works 7 days; no reminders, no texts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They agree to the video recording first and check their camera and microphone (a preview and a sound level). Then nine questions from the role&#39;s rubric: experience, the role&#39;s skills, social media, what CarmaCars does and the shift, the role&#39;s scenario, the hours and the pay, internet and backup, education and other jobs, career and moving to Canada. Each is shown and read aloud; then the answer time counts down (2 minutes by default) and they press Record when ready. Recording stops by itself at 0:00 and the answer is sent; the clock turns red for the last 15 seconds. Every answer is on video and spoken, nothing is typed, and the English question is spoken too. Where an answer is vague the AI asks a short follow-up, two at most.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the last answer is in, the candidate is <b class="gd-ui">Interviewed</b>. Within minutes the AI scores each rubric line 1 to 5 with a quote from the answers, scores every answer out of 10 with a one-line reason, judges the spoken English, lists anything to check, and recommends: <b class="gd-ui">Invite to a live call</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Hire</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Good fit for Sales instead</b>. Hiring shows &quot;N AI interviews done and waiting for your decision&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Open the candidate. The AI interview card has the recommendation and the scores, then every answer in order: its video, the transcript, the AI&#39;s score for that rubric line and the answer&#39;s score out of 10. <b class="gd-ui">Watch all</b> plays every video one after the other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The interview decides by itself (release 41, on by default again since release 44): a pass needs all of these: the score at or over the bar (80 of 100 unless you change it in <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b>), no knock-out answer, the answers averaging 7 or more out of 10 with none under 5, and spoken English judged good or fluent. A Sales applicant who passes is hired with one-step Hire and starts with the academy. Every other role that passes (customer service, fleet, finance and field) is invited to book an interview date. Under the bar, or with any knock-out answer, the decline email or the Sales referral goes, once. You can still press <b class="gd-ui">Invite to a live call</b> on any candidate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A link that expired: <b class="gd-ui">New interview link</b> emails a new one for 7 days; the answers given are kept.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>You are told, never asked: an alert for each new applicant and each finished interview, with the score, the bar and what happened. Only a booked live call needs you: it is an alert and a To-do at the call time. <b class="gd-ui">Interview settings</b> holds the bar, the follow-up questions (4) and <b class="gd-ui">Decide by hand</b> if you ever want to decide yourself. Transcripts and scores use the free Workers AI allowance (Settings &gt; Usage, &quot;Hiring interviews&quot;); when today&#39;s share is used, the answer is kept and the transcript or the scores come later by themselves. The videos are deleted after 90 days (the sound and the transcript stay); everything else is deleted with the application, 12 months after the decision.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-redo-the-ai-interview" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Redo the AI interview</h2><p class="gd-p">If an interview went badly for a reason that is not the applicant&#39;s (a broken camera, a lost connection), open the candidate and press <b class="gd-ui">Redo the AI interview</b>, then confirm.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Their staff access ends if they were already hired.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The old interview and its answers are kept as history on the candidate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The application goes back to <b class="gd-ui">Invited</b> and a new interview link is emailed, good for 7 days.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A redone interview follows the same pass rule as any other: only a Sales applicant who passes is hired by itself.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-phone-or-video-and-the-remote-calls-confirmed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone or video, and the remote calls confirmed</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The way a call is held follows the role: Field staff and Sales in person are called by phone (record it with Quo), the remote roles meet by video (a Jitsi link in their emails). An interview day&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">How</b> is only the default shown.</li><li>Remote candidates get no reminders and no texts. 24 hours before the call (at once if they book closer than that) they get one email with <b class="gd-ui">Confirm my call</b> (one press, no sign-in). Not confirmed within 12 hours of that email, or by 1 hour before the call, the call is cancelled, the time opens again and they get a short email with the link to book again.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Calls</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Confirmed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Waiting</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Asked 24 hours before</b> for each remote call, and <b class="gd-ui">Cancelled: not confirmed</b> for the last 7 days. The in-person roles keep their reminders.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-hire-from-any-stage-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Hire from any stage (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> is on every candidate who is not hired yet, a candidate referred to another role included: choose the role in the form and confirm. No booking link is sent. After the hire you get one alert: &quot;&lt;name&gt; hired as &lt;role&gt;, starts &lt;date&gt;, training not started&quot;, which opens their academy progress.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-every-applicant-into-sales" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Every applicant into Sales</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A closed role&#39;s page says the role is filled and sends the applicant to the Sales application (remote, or in person for an in-person role), with their name and email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The Program setting to refer VA applicants to Sales (on by default): every customer service, Fleet or Finance applicant gets the Sales referral email; those already waiting get it from the hiring job.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every role takes the AI video interview, the in-person roles too (field staff are asked about driving and car care, and getting around Toronto); a phone call stays optional.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A Sales applicant whose AI interview score meets the auto-hire mark (Program settings; empty means the interview&#39;s pass mark: passing means hired) is hired by itself with one-step Hire: the account, the agreement, the academy with the gate, the welcome. You get an alert for each. Below the mark, you decide as before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The Hire form&#39;s standard pay reads the role&#39;s own pay (its amount, or the amount in its pay text), so it matches the careers page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-in-person-needs-the-toronto-area-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">In person needs the Toronto area (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">An in-person role asks where the applicant lives: city, province or state, and country. Only these are used, with the country of the phone number and of the connection. The area is a Program setting (100 km of Toronto by default).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">An applicant outside the area is told so and offered Remote Sales with their name and email filled in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The list and the candidate page show <b class="gd-ui">Lives in</b>, flag <b class="gd-ui">Location mismatch</b> when the phone or the connection is from another country, and offer <b class="gd-ui">Move to Remote Sales</b> to an in-person Sales applicant outside Canada.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hire</b> chooses Sales remote for a candidate outside the area, and refuses Sales in person for them.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-dates-before-the-townhall-release-35-widened-in-re" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview dates before the townhall (release 35, widened in release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every role has the AI interview. A Sales applicant who passes is hired by itself. An applicant for any other role who passes is invited to a 10-minute interview date: six slots in the hour before the weekly townhall (Wednesday 12:00 to 13:00), opened each week, booked from their usual link with the usual reminders. The slots are on <b class="gd-ui">Calls</b> here and on the Fleet home page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-interview-call-reminders-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Interview call reminders (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">For every booked interview call you get an alert the morning of (9:00 am, the day&#39;s calls), an hour before the first call of the day, and 10 minutes before each call with the candidate, the role and the call link (or <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> for a phone call). <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Interviews today</b>: each call&#39;s time, candidate, role and its <b class="gd-ui">Join</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> button. The interview is harder than before: questions on reliability, a typed customer message (written English) and, for Sales, an objection to answer, with up to 4 probing follow-ups. It is the pre-screen to the academy.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-the-sales-funnel-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Sales funnel (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">The Pipeline tab opens with <b class="gd-ui">Sales funnel</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Sales staff in the academy</b>: how many have not started, are in progress or are done, and how many have made no progress for 2 days. Each person on the Academy step shows &quot;Academy 3 of 19 (Sales), last active 2 days ago&quot;. A hired person with no academy progress is reminded on day 1, 2 and 4 (an alert and an email); the 5-day suspension follows.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The re-send</b>: once, every applicant referred to Sales who never applied got the referral again as <b class="gd-ui">Yes, put me in Sales</b>, and every Sales applicant who never finished the AI interview got a fresh link. One email per address, a few every 15 minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The bar for Sales</b>: a Sales applicant passes the AI interview at or over the bar (Interview settings, 80 by default) with no knock-out answer, English not basic and no answer under 4 out of 10; the AI&#39;s recommendation no longer declines a Sales applicant over the bar. Sales applicants declined that way in the last 30 days were decided again. Auto-hire still needs a passed AI interview.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A red box says when a WhatsApp group link is empty: nobody can join until you set it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'advertising-and-owner-recruitment', 'chapter', 'academy', 'Marketing writes the text of every ad from the car''s own record, keeps track of where each ad is posted, tells the sales assistants when an ad needs updating, shows which channels bring bookings, drafts the week''s Facebook Page and Instagram posts and keeps the consent log for owner recruitment. Nothing is posted by the server: you post by hand, and Facebook Marketplace from the owner''s own profile, with a kit and a daily rotation under Marketplace.

## Facebook Marketplace

**Marketing** > **Marketplace**. Listings go up from the owner''s own Facebook profile (business Pages cannot post vehicles), by Claude in the owner''s Chrome or by a person. The playbook is docs/runbooks/marketplace.md.

1. **Today** lists what is due: **Update the price** and **Take down** first, then up to the day''s allowance of new posts and renewals (4 a day by default: 3 to 5 a day avoids spam flags). **Coming up** shows the next days.
2. Press **Kit** on a car. The kit shows every field of facebook.com/marketplace/create/vehicle in the form''s order (location, year, make, model, mileage, price, body style, colours, condition, fuel, transmission), each with **Copy**, the description in Marketplace style, and the tracked link.
3. Press **Download the photos (ZIP)**. It has the 10 best photos named 01 to 10. Add them in that order: the first is the cover.
4. Post it. Then press **Posted** on Today and paste the listing''s address. Press **Renewed**, **Updated** or **Taken down** the same way when you do those.
5. **Inbox replies for this car** has the answers for price, availability, requirements, deposit, delivery and "send your number", filled in for the car. Each one ends with the car''s link or asks for a phone number.
6. After answering the inbox, open **Log an inbox session**. Enter the number of chats and the numbers collected, one per line (name, phone, car code). Each new number becomes a lead, and customer service gets a call-back task due within 15 minutes.

- Kits are made when the page opens, so their prices are today''s. A price change marks the live listing **Update the price** and opens the usual update task.
- A car that does not take requests, has no daily rate or has only sample photos says **Do not post yet**.
- **Rotation settings** change the posts a day, the days before a renewal, and the default location (a car''s home area wins).
- **The team''s listings**: Sales post from their own profiles under **Sales** > **Marketing**, each listing in its own copy variant (title, description, photo order and cover), so no ad is posted twice. A car has at most 5 live listings, yours included (**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Facebook Marketplace**). The card lists who posted what, its status, when it ends and the listing''s address. Your own posts and renewals still count against your own day only.
- The booking request asks "How did you hear about us?" (optional). Bookings by channel counts the answer after staff''s source and a tracked visit.

## Write an ad

**Marketing** > **Ads**, the **Ad listings** tab.

1. Choose the car and the channel (Facebook Marketplace, Kijiji, Craigslist, Instagram, Facebook Page or Google Business Profile) and press **Write it**.
2. Copy each part with its button: the title, the price line, the description (or caption), the hashtags and the tracked link. Each shows its length against the channel''s limit (a Kijiji title takes 64 characters, Craigslist 70, an Instagram caption 2,200, a Google post 1,500).
3. Add the photos in the order shown: the first is the cover. Open a photo to save it.
4. Post the ad on the site, then press **Mark as posted** and paste its address and the date.

- The text comes from the car''s record only: the rates, kilometres, deposit, delivery fee, who may rent it and the car code. A fact the record does not have is left out. No review, rating or claim is added.
- The tracked link opens the car''s page with utm_source (the channel), utm_medium and utm_campaign (the car code), so the request counts under that channel.
- A warning shows when the car does not take requests, has no daily rate, or shows sample photos (take real photos first: an ad shows the car itself).
- Facebook Marketplace is posted from the owner''s own Facebook profile in their browser: Meta does not take vehicle listings from business Pages. Kijiji takes one ad per car, in one category and one region. An Instagram caption cannot hold a working link: put it in the bio or a story link sticker.

## When an ad needs updating

**Marketing** > **Posted ads**, or the task in **Today** > **Staff tasks**.

1. A change of 3% or more in a car''s daily, weekend, weekly or 30-day rate, any change of its deposit, kilometres, extra-km price or delivery fee, or the car leaving the site marks each of its live ads Needs updating and opens a task for the sales assistants (for example Update the Kijiji ad and the car). The task says what changed, the new price line and the ad''s address.
2. Press **New text**, copy the new text and update the ad on the site.
3. Press **Mark the ad updated**. The task closes. Closing the task in Staff tasks counts too.
4. Car off the site: take the ad down and press **Taken down**. If the car comes back at the same rates first, the task is cancelled by itself.

> Good to know: The 3% is under **Settings** > **Program**, Advertising and owner recruitment. The rates are checked again every 6 hours, so a rate dated ahead is caught on its day.

## Bookings by channel

**Marketing** > **Bookings by channel**.

- Every request of the dates chosen counts once: under the source staff set on the booking, else the renter''s visit (the campaign source of a tracked link, or the site they came from), else a referral code, else how it reached us (phone, email, WhatsApp).
- Choose the last visit before the request or the first visit. A booking is a request that was confirmed, paid or completed; revenue is its rental charge after discounts. The months add up to the Bookings list.
- The visit is kept with the request when it is sent, so the source outlives the 90 days of visit history. A visitor who refused analytics cookies has no source.
- On a booking, the line Came from shows the source. Press **Set** to give it by hand when the renter told you (a Kijiji reply, a walk-in, word of mouth).

## Facebook Page and Instagram drafts

**Marketing** > **Social drafts**.

1. The week''s drafts are written from the fleet every 6 hours, for this week and the next: Monday a new car (published in the last 14 days) or a featured one; Tuesday the owner program; Thursday the cars free this weekend; Friday the requirements (Instagram); Sunday a price highlight or a seasonal trip (Facebook Page). Press **Write drafts for this week** to write them now.
2. Read each draft. Press **Edit** to change the caption, the channels or the day, then **Approve**; or press **Skip**.
3. Copy the caption for each channel (on the Facebook Page the tracked link is in the text; for Instagram copy the link for the bio), post it with the photos shown, then press **Posted on Instagram** or **Posted on Facebook Page** and paste the post''s address.

- Wednesday''s walkaround video and Saturday''s handover story are filmed by field staff. No renter is shown without written consent.
- Press **Add a post of your own** at the bottom of the week for anything else.

## Meta publishing (off until set up)

**Settings** > **Meta publishing**. Until it is on, every post is copied and posted by hand.

1. Make the Instagram account a professional account and link it to the CarmaCars Facebook Page.
2. At developers.facebook.com, create a Business app owned by the CarmaCars business portfolio. Give it the permissions pages_show_list, pages_read_engagement, pages_manage_posts, instagram_basic and instagram_content_publish, and make a long-lived Page access token. Meta may ask for App Review before posts are public.
3. Press **Enter the details**: the Page id, the Instagram account id and the token. The token goes to the vault; the page shows only its last four characters.
4. Press **Switch on**. Approved drafts then go out on their day and their post links are recorded; a refusal shows on the draft. Press **Switch off** or **Remove the token** at any time.

## Scheduled posts (Facebook, Instagram, TikTok)

**Marketing** > **Social drafts**, the Scheduled posts card at the top. Sales have the same card on their Marketing page.

1. Choose where (Facebook Page, Instagram or TikTok) and when. Pick a draft for its caption and link (and its photo), or write the caption. Pick a short video if you made one. Press **Schedule**.
2. Every 5 minutes the database marks the posts whose time has come as due. With Meta publishing switched on, Facebook and Instagram posts go out by themselves (photos, Page videos and Instagram reels) and the post link is recorded; Meta refusing three times makes the post Failed with Meta''s answer and a Try again button.
3. Without Meta publishing the card says **Connect Meta** and works as a queue: at its time a post is due with the caption to copy and the photo or video to download. Post it, then press **Posted by hand** and paste the post''s address.
4. TikTok is always by hand (its posting API needs TikTok''s app review): a due TikTok post shows the checklist. Download the video, post it in the TikTok app with the caption, copy the link, press **Posted by hand**.

- Instagram needs a photo or an MP4 video; TikTok needs a video. Every change is in the post''s Log.
- Facebook Marketplace has no posting API: keep using the Marketplace kit and its session flow.

## Short video for Reels, TikTok and Stories

On a listing (below First photo) or in **Marketing** > **Marketplace**, the car''s kit.

1. Press **Make a short video**. Your browser draws a 9:16 video from the car''s approved photos: a slow zoom on each, the brand at the top, the car, the price a day and the call to action at the bottom. Keep the tab in front until it says Saved (about 20 seconds for 8 photos).
2. Press **Download** to post it yourself, or schedule it in Scheduled posts. **Remove** takes it off the list.

> Good to know: The words and timing are **Settings** > **Program**: social video call to action ({price} is the live price a day), brand, seconds a photo and photos a video. It is free: nothing is sent to a paid service.

## Make the missing angle

On a listing (below First photo) or in the Marketplace kit: for a required angle the car has no photo of.

1. Press **Make Rear** (or the angle missing). The image model makes that view from the car''s approved photos, only within its free daily use (the showroom''s limit).
2. Check the view: same car, same colour, wheels and badges, no damage hidden or added. Press **Approve** or **Reject**.

> Watch out: An approved view shows on the site after the real photos, labelled AI view. It is never the cover and never used as damage or condition evidence (handovers, claims). Take the real photo when you can: a real photo of the angle replaces the view at once.

## Owner recruitment

**Marketing** > **Owner recruitment**.

Owners and co-hosts are found in classified ads. The anti-spam law (CASL) does not cover a live phone call, but an email or a text needs consent, names the sender and offers an unsubscribe. The lawyer confirms the approach before outreach starts.

1. Press **Add a lead**: paste the ad''s address, choose who is selling (a private seller, a dealer or a rental business) and type the name, the phone and the car from the ad. Nothing is collected from the classified site.
2. Call them with the script on the lead''s page and press **Log the call**. A yes needs their words ("Yes, text me the details"): they become express consent in the log. A no means do not contact, ever.
3. When the lead''s page says email or text is allowed, choose a template, check the words and press **Send**. The email adds CarmaCars'' name, mailing address and the unsubscribe link; the text ends with "Reply STOP to opt out." Texts wait for 8 am during quiet hours.

- Press **Record consent** for consent given another way: express (with its proof), implied by their inquiry (6 months), implied by a business relationship (2 years), a business address published with no "no solicitation" note (never a private seller), or one message after a referral (naming the referrer).
- The consent log is never edited: a change is a new line. An unsubscribe or a STOP reply adds a withdrawal by itself, and nothing more goes on that channel.
- A message without consent is refused with the reason. **Settings** > **Program** has a switch that stops all recruitment messages.

> Watch out: Keep the proof of an oral yes: a recording, or a note written during the call with the time. Consent you cannot show does not count.


## Owner pipeline

Open **Marketing** > **Owner pipeline**. Every prospective owner is one card, in one of eight columns: New, Contacted, Call booked, Applied, Agreement sent, Signed, Car onboarded and Lost. Leads come from the owner form on the website, an owner''s referral link, Owner recruitment (classified ads) and **Add an owner lead**. A visitor who starts the application is a lead as soon as a valid email or mobile is typed (Website form, unfinished), with the car they entered or priced in the earnings calculator; the same email or phone joins the lead already open.

1. Follow-up emails go by themselves on day 0, 2, 5 and 10 after a lead comes in: the owner program in plain words (the car goes on our fleet insurance policy, we rent it out in Toronto and pay the owner every month; fees apply) and the link to apply. They are marketing emails: they wait behind every other email under the daily limit, go in the sending hours and carry the unsubscribe link.
2. They go only with consent: a website inquiry counts for 6 months, a classified-ad lead needs consent in its log, and a referral typed by staff gets one message only.
3. They stop when the lead replies (a text or a call from their number, or press **They replied**), when the stage changes, when they unsubscribe, and after the last one. **Stop follow-ups** and **Restart follow-ups** are on each card.
4. **Move** changes the stage (with a note, and why when lost). Agreement sent, Signed and Car onboarded also follow the owner''s records: an owner agreement sent or signed, a car on the site.
5. Customer service sees the same board in the staff portal. Sales see only the owners they invited, added or were given, on My sales.
6. A new website lead goes to the least busy Sales person, never to a verification or test account (with no real Sales person on, it waits unassigned). Test accounts are never "sourced by" on a real lead or owner, nor given its task.
7. An application left unfinished for 30 minutes goes to the least busy Sales person with a task, and its follow-ups say "finish your application" with a link that opens their saved answers. When they send it, the card moves to Applied and the follow-ups stop.
8. Leads that came in before the automatic follow-ups existed and that nobody moved are in To do as a task "Follow up now" with their name: call or email them, then move the card.

### Owner referral links

An owner''s link for new owners is `carmacars.ca/r/<their code>?to=owner` (the list is at the bottom of the board). A new owner who applies after it is credited to that owner. The credit follows the referral kickback rule: the Kickback Rate (20%) of the Rental Charge of the first completed rental of the new owner''s car. It shows under **Owner referral credits** as due; pay it with the owner''s payout and press **Mark paid**.

## Listing channels

Open **Marketing** > **Listing channels**: the sites and directories where our cars can be listed beyond carmacars.ca (Turo, Getaround, Google Business Profile, Google Merchant Center, the Meta catalog, Kijiji, Facebook Marketplace, KAYAK, Expedia, Discover Cars, Rentalcars.com, Craigslist, Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp, YellowPages and any you add).

1. Each has a status (Not started, Applied, Live, Paused, Not for us), who holds the login, notes and how listing works there. Press **Update** to change them, **Add a channel** for a new one.
2. None is connected by itself: apply on the site. When a site or partner program takes a feed, give it that channel''s address: **JSON**, **CSV** or **XML** (the XML is in the shape of Google''s vehicle listings feed). Car links carry the channel, so its bookings show in Bookings by channel.
3. Every feed has our own and co-hosted cars on the site, never a partner''s car (01 Motors or any other). **Keep out** takes a car out of every feed.
4. **New key** ends the old address. Each feed is read at most 60 times an hour and each answer is kept 15 minutes.

## Email campaigns

**Marketing** > **Channels** > **Email campaigns**. Everyone who gave us their email address on carmacars.ca gets the marketing emails: renters, customer accounts, leads from the site''s forms and addresses typed into forms that were never sent. Staff, owners as owners, Turo guests and leads typed in by staff are left out. Anyone who unsubscribes is never emailed again: the link is in every marketing email and takes effect at once.

1. **Audience** is how many addresses may be emailed now; **Waiting**, **Queued**, **Sent** and **Unsubscribed** follow.
2. **The weekly email** goes on the day and hour set below, with the cars listed now and the public promo codes running now.
3. **A new car**: when a car''s listing goes live (never a sample car), everyone gets one email about it, once.
4. Marketing emails go after every booking, payment and sign-in email, within the free daily email budgets (Cloudflare first, then Resend''s free plan). With **Send more marketing automatically** on, marketing uses what is left after the reserve; what does not fit waits for the next day. One campaign email a person a day at most.
5. **Switches and timing**: each campaign on or off, the day and hour of the weekly email, the reserve. Saving writes a new dated row of Program settings.', 'Advertising and owner recruitment', 'Ad text for each car and channel, posted ads and their update tasks, bookings by channel, social drafts, Meta publishing, owner recruitment and its consent log, and the email campaigns to everyone who gave us their email.',
  'Marketing writes the text of every ad from the car''s own record, keeps track of where each ad is posted, tells the sales assistants when an ad needs updating, shows which channels bring bookings, drafts the week''s Facebook Page and Instagram posts and keeps the consent log for owner recruitment. Nothing is posted by the server: you post by hand, and Facebook Marketplace from the owner''s own profile, with a kit and a daily rotation under Marketplace.

## Facebook Marketplace

**Marketing** > **Marketplace**. Listings go up from the owner''s own Facebook profile (business Pages cannot post vehicles), by Claude in the owner''s Chrome or by a person. The playbook is docs/runbooks/marketplace.md.

1. **Today** lists what is due: **Update the price** and **Take down** first, then up to the day''s allowance of new posts and renewals (4 a day by default: 3 to 5 a day avoids spam flags). **Coming up** shows the next days.
2. Press **Kit** on a car. The kit shows every field of facebook.com/marketplace/create/vehicle in the form''s order (location, year, make, model, mileage, price, body style, colours, condition, fuel, transmission), each with **Copy**, the description in Marketplace style, and the tracked link.
3. Press **Download the photos (ZIP)**. It has the 10 best photos named 01 to 10. Add them in that order: the first is the cover.
4. Post it. Then press **Posted** on Today and paste the listing''s address. Press **Renewed**, **Updated** or **Taken down** the same way when you do those.
5. **Inbox replies for this car** has the answers for price, availability, requirements, deposit, delivery and "send your number", filled in for the car. Each one ends with the car''s link or asks for a phone number.
6. After answering the inbox, open **Log an inbox session**. Enter the number of chats and the numbers collected, one per line (name, phone, car code). Each new number becomes a lead, and customer service gets a call-back task due within 15 minutes.

- Kits are made when the page opens, so their prices are today''s. A price change marks the live listing **Update the price** and opens the usual update task.
- A car that does not take requests, has no daily rate or has only sample photos says **Do not post yet**.
- **Rotation settings** change the posts a day, the days before a renewal, and the default location (a car''s home area wins).
- **The team''s listings**: Sales post from their own profiles under **Sales** > **Marketing**, each listing in its own copy variant (title, description, photo order and cover), so no ad is posted twice. A car has at most 5 live listings, yours included (**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Facebook Marketplace**). The card lists who posted what, its status, when it ends and the listing''s address. Your own posts and renewals still count against your own day only.
- The booking request asks "How did you hear about us?" (optional). Bookings by channel counts the answer after staff''s source and a tracked visit.

